  "question_origin": "researcher_constructed",
  "question_text": "A competitive market has inverse demand P = 50 - Q and inverse supply P = 10 + Q. Supply equals marginal private cost, and demand equals marginal social benefit. Production creates a constant marginal external cost of $10 per unit. There are no other externalities. P is dollars per unit and Q is units per day.\n(a) Calculate the unregulated market equilibrium price and quantity. Show your work.\n(b) Calculate the socially efficient quantity and explain the efficiency condition you use.\n(c) State the per-unit corrective tax that would implement the efficient quantity.\n(d) Draw a correctly labeled graph showing demand, marginal private cost, marginal social cost, the unregulated quantity, and the socially efficient quantity.",
