      "answer": {
        "answer_markdown": "### (a) Unregulated equilibrium\nSet demand equal to private supply:\n\\[\n50-Q=10+Q \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad 40=2Q \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad Q_m=20.\n\\]\nSubstitute into either curve: \\(P_m=50-20=\\$30\\) per unit.\n\n### (b) Socially efficient quantity\nMarginal social cost includes the $10 external cost:\n\\[\nMSC=MPC+MEC=(10+Q)+10=20+Q.\n\\]\nEfficiency requires **marginal social benefit to equal marginal social cost** (\\(MSB=MSC\\)):\n\\[\n50-Q=20+Q \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad Q^*=15.\n\\]\n\n### (c) Corrective tax\nA tax of **$10 per unit** makes producers face the full marginal social cost and implements \\(Q^*=15\\).\n\n### (d) Graph\n",
