        "answer_markdown": "### (a) Unregulated market equilibrium\nSet demand equal to private supply:\n\\[\n50-Q=10+Q \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad 40=2Q \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad Q_m=20.\n\\]\nSubstitute into either curve:\n\\[\nP_m=50-20=\\boxed{\\$30\\text{ per unit}}.\n\\]\nThus the unregulated equilibrium is \\(\\boxed{(Q_m,P_m)=(20,\\$30)}\\).\n\n### (b) Socially efficient quantity\nMarginal social cost includes the $10 external cost:\n\\[\nMSC=MPC+10=(10+Q)+10=20+Q.\n\\]\nEfficiency requires marginal social benefit to equal marginal social cost (\\(MSB=MSC\\)):\n\\[\n50-Q=20+Q \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad Q^*=\\boxed{15\\text{ units per day}}.\n\\]\n\n### (c) Corrective tax\nA per-unit tax equal to marginal external cost implements the efficient quantity: \\(\\boxed{\\$10\\text{ per unit}}\\).",
